.TH EASYDNS 8 "November 2026" "EasyDNS 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
easydns \- internal DNS server with optional native peering
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B easydns
.RB [ \-c " configuration" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
EasyDNS serves local zones and forwards other DNS queries to upstream
servers. Native authenticated peering can replicate zones between nodes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " FILE"
Read YAML configuration from FILE.
The default is /etc/easydns/easydns.yaml.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/easydns/easydns.yaml
Server configuration, preserved across package upgrades.
.TP
.I /var/cache/easydns/state.yaml
Default saved zone state.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/easydns/examples/
Example hierarchical and native peering configurations.
.SH LOGGING
The packaged configuration uses syslog, falling back to standard output
when /dev/log is unavailable. The systemd service captures standard
output in the journal. Set logging.file to /var/log/easydns.log to also
write a log file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)